    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for the Austin Waves presents a challenging environment, as our active roster is forced to contend with Cease, a formidable arm boasting a 2.96 xERA. Consequently, our offensive output is projected to be tempered, with **Drake Baldwin** and **Andy Pages** operating as marginal plays at 40.51 and 43.41, respectively. While **Andy Pages** earns a slight edge due to his proximity to the heart of the order relative to **Drake Baldwin**\u2014who suffers a significant efficiency penalty batting ninth\u2014both remain locked into the lineup purely to maintain our 5x5 category floor. The structural disadvantage of facing a top-tier pitcher like Cease effectively suppresses the offensive ceiling for these two, making them volume-dependent starts rather than high-conviction anchors.\n\nThe bench remains stagnant today due to a league-wide scheduling quirk, as heavy hitters like **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** are all inactive. The most pressing concern for our front office remains the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who continues to occupy a roster spot while on the IL; his absence creates a vacuum in our speed profile that we are currently unable to fill with the likes of **Nasim Nunez** or **Cole Carrigg**. Looking ahead, we need **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Josh Lowe** to provide the necessary catalysts once they return to action, as our current depth options\u2014including **Jacob Wilson**, **Jorge Polanco**, and **Heliot Ramos**\u2014are currently lacking the situational leverage required to outperform today\u2019s suppressed projections. We will monitor the health of **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, and **Miguel Vargas** closely, as any deviation in their recovery timelines will necessitate a more aggressive reshuffling of our bench depth against upcoming weaker rotations.",
